# Helix Shell restart

After changes that need a **running** shell update, prefer a soft path first:

1. Rebuild the binary (`cargo build --profile fast` / `--release`).
2. Run `tools/switch-shell.sh install` to refresh symlinks and units **without** restarting if the shell is already active.

Prefer bouncing **panels only** when the change is Overlay UI (Mobius dropdown, launcher, CC, …):

```sh
./tools/switch-shell.sh restart-panels
```

That keeps the bar and the exclusive-zone strut up and avoids crashing Cursor.

Bounce the **painted bar** when bar chrome / Shell1 / dock code changed:

```sh
./tools/switch-shell.sh restart-bar
```

The strut (`helix-shell-strut`) stays mapped, so niri work area should not flap. Still prefer a plain terminal outside Cursor if unsure.

Full pair (bar + panels, strut stays):

```sh
./tools/switch-shell.sh restart
```

**Do not** bounce the strut as a routine step while Cursor is open — tearing down `helix-shell-reserve` flaps work area and has crashed Cursor. Only use `restart-strut` when the strut binary or `BAR_HEIGHT` itself changed, from a terminal outside Cursor.

The C++ `helix-shell-dev.service` unit is retired; do not restart it.
